Abstract = {social media has allowed anybody to share their opinions and engage with
   the general public, but it has also become a platform for harsh
   language, cruel conduct, personal assaults, and cyberbullying. However,
   determining whether a comment or a post is violent or not remains
   difficult and time-consuming, and most social media businesses are
   always seeking better ways to do so. This may be automated to assist in
   detecting nasty comments, promote user safety, preserve websites, and
   enhance online dialogue. The toxic comment dataset is utilized in this
   research to train a deep learning model that categorizes comments into
   the following categories: severe toxic, toxic, threat, obscene, insult,
   and identity hatred. To categorize comments, use a bidirectional long
   short-term memory cell (Bi-LSTM).},
